TEXT 536 112 Left 2 ;The conservated (stored)  inductive energy\nwork after switchoff in the load devices
TEXT 280 120 Left 2 ;Hard switching:\ntoff=1u vt=0.9 vh=0
TEXT 536 176 Left 2 ;This load is only for let\nthe current flow after\nswitching off
TEXT 392 232 Left 2 ;NOTE: At a real world circuit the breaker acts a lot more smoother at switching\ntherefore there are normally only small voltage spikes present !!!!\nVoltage spikes in this simulation are because the energy and current cannot be suddenly\nat zero level. Since after switching off (with our hard switcher) )current flow now through\nthe suddenly high "off resistance" of the breaker. So the energy is killed in the\nbreaker resistance. (E=I*I*R) and the voltage gives values about TeraVolt
TEXT -328 -72 Left 2 ;Small simulation range because \nof zooming to the switching time\nis only possible if x-axis is in ns
TEXT 544 -72 Left 2 ;Shows the conservated energy inside the short circuit limiting reactance\nIntegrate one halvewave of power V(N001)\nbefore 500ms (multiply trace with *1W/1V and STRG+Click afterwards)
TEXT 840 120 Left 2 ;This high load is like shorting\nthe line
TEXT 72 -120 Left 2 ;Shows the powerflow from transformer to switcher\nat switching time (It is the same as ALT/(ALT Gr)+Click on the\ndevice \n ( NOTE: ALT+click on german keyboard layout often crash LTspice\nPlease use ALT Gr + Click for german keyboards )\nDon't forget to multiply the trace by 1W/1V before CTRL+Click on the traces\nThe energyflow from transformer to switcher\nat switching time  is about 3.8kJ (only the right side\nof the transormer energy is used)
TEXT 720 8 Left 2 ;The line in between reactor and load is\nassumed very short and so is neglected
TEXT 464 192 Left 2 !.param pn1=1e6
TEXT -320 248 Left 2 ;Breakpoint device \nfor higher simulation resolution\nat switching time\nHINT: You can also insert more than one\nBreakpoint devices with different stepsizes
TEXT -328 -144 Left 5 ;This example shows the energyflow from the transformer\nto the switcher at switching off
TEXT 464 -152 Left 5 ;For the energy flow from the short circuit limiting reactor\nto the two loads see also the file\nInductive_Energy_ShortCircuitReactor.asc
TEXT -328 -104 Left 2 ;After simulation open the .plt file\nInductive_Energy_ShortCircuitReactor_with_Energymeter.plt\nto see the optimal zooming level
